// A client comes up, and stays up, with whatever optional mods it was started with. This is the check
// 1.0.9 lacked: every NeoForge client without Sophisticated Core crashed on startup, and nothing saw it,
// because runClient always has every optional mod. Leave mods out with -PwithoutOptional:
//     ./gradlew ":<node>:runClient" -Pagent=tools/agent/smoke/boot.jsonl -PwithoutOptional=all
//     ./gradlew ":<node>:runClient" -Pagent=tools/agent/smoke/boot.jsonl -PwithoutOptional=sophisticated-core
// The second shape, one mod gone and Jade still there, is the one 1.0.9 crashed in: Jade loads every
// plugin it is given whether or not the mod the plugin is for is installed.
//
// It asks for nothing a title screen cannot answer, so it runs as it is, and with -Pquickplay=<world>
// it also opens that world, loads the chunks round the player and draws the HUD before it stops,
// and fails when the world never opened. Then verify what it recorded:
//     python tools/agent/drive.py run/<node>/agent/client tools/agent/smoke/boot.jsonl --verify --max-age 10
// A crash fails the Gradle task: a Fabric client exits on its own, and a driven NeoForge client exits
// from the loading error screen rather than waiting on it. It also leaves the previous run's queue
// behind, which is what --max-age is for: without it, verify would read that run's answers and pass.

{"id": "probe", "command": "probe", "expect": {"ok": true, "result.side": "client"}}
{"id": "settle", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 200}}
{"id": "info", "command": "client.info", "expect": {"ok": true}}
// Long enough for a quickplay world to finish joining and tick with the player in it.
{"id": "play", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 400}}
// With -Pquickplay the client must be inside that world by now. A world that fails to open, as every
// world did with Cold Sweat and without Farmer's Delight in 1.4.0, drops back to a menu and leaves the
// game running, so answering at all proves nothing. Without -Pquickplay this is always false.
{"id": "still", "command": "client.info", "expect": {"ok": true, "result.quickplayFailed": false}}
